@jhonabreul @Marinovsky @Martin-Molinero Hi, Unfortrunately I think this bug is still present. I think if you look at the expected result, it should be that `warm_up_indicator` has the indicator ready to go from the first bar of trading. It shouldn't be zero or incorrect, which it still is. This is still happening when running the test. I also tested the macd and found that to be wrong from the first trade bar, but by the end of the month had normalised to almost the same value, which points again to an issue in `warm_up_indicator` that is greater than just the stochastic indicator. 

For me, this means essentially that `warm_up_indicator` cannot be used in any code. At least they way it is coded in this issue, unless there is another way to use it that gives accurate results?

